(Arithmetic in Vox is said in words: add, subtract, multiply, divide and
 modulo. Each line below reads the sum aloud, then works it out in braces.)

Print "Whole numbers".

Set apples to 10.
Set pears to 3.

Print "The bowl holds 10 apples and 3 pears.".
Print "".

Print "Pieces of fruit altogether, apples add pears: {apples add pears}".

Print "How many more apples than pears, apples subtract pears: {apples subtract pears}".

Print "Ways to pick one apple and one pear, apples multiply pears: {apples multiply pears}".

Print "Apples for each pear, apples divide pears: {apples divide pears}".

Print "Apples left over, apples modulo pears: {apples modulo pears}".

Print "".
Print "Decimals".

Set length to 10.5.
Set width to 3.2.

Print "The room is 10.5 metres long and 3.2 metres wide.".
Print "".

(A decimal is a 64-bit float, so a sum like 10.5 add 3.2 shows the
 rounding of its last binary digit)
Print "Half the way around the walls, length add width: {length add width}".

Print "How much longer than wide, length subtract width: {length subtract width}".

Print "Floor area, length multiply width: {length multiply width}".

Print "How many widths make the length, length divide width: {length divide width}".

Print "".
Print "One value, changed step by step".

Set flour to 5.0.
Print "The recipe starts with 5.0 cups of flour.".

Set flour to flour add 2.5.
Print "After adding 2.5 cups: {flour}".

Set flour to flour multiply 2.0.
Print "After doubling the recipe: {flour}".

Set flour to flour subtract 3.0.
Print "After setting 3.0 cups aside: {flour}".

Set flour to flour divide 2.0.
Print "Shared between two bowls, each bowl holds: {flour}".

Print "".
Print "Comparisons".

If length is greater than 10.0 then, print "The room is more than 10 metres long.".
Otherwise, print "The room is 10 metres long or less.".

If width is less than 3.5 then, print "It is narrower than 3.5 metres.".
Otherwise, print "It is 3.5 metres wide or more.".

If flour is equal to 6.0 then, print "Each bowl holds exactly 6.0 cups.".
Otherwise, print "The bowls hold something other than 6.0 cups.".

Print "".
Print "Counting with a decimal".
Print "A five-kilometre walk, one marker at a time:".
Set kilometres to 0.0.
While kilometres is less than 5.0,
    Print kilometres,
    Set kilometres to kilometres add 1.0.

Print "".
Print "Done!".
